{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZeuX7FLSQvfMZXxDZQZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 09 (PLA folding) is done. Table 1's \"equivalent up to ±1\" claim is false for PLA folding as Möhring defines it, and the gap is unbounded. The gate passes: `lake build` is ok, there is no new `sorry`, and 1,231 tests pass.\n\nThe work is in `lean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PLAFolding.lean`, imported from the root file. It has no `sorry`, and it depends only on the standard axioms (`propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).\n\n- **Definition (Möhring p. 25, PLAMPP):** a PLA layout is a gate matrix track assignment (from item 03) with at most `c` nets per track. `plaTracks` is the case `c = 2`. With no real cap (`c` at least the number of nets) it is multiple folding.\n- **The correct relation, proved:** PLA tracks ≥ max(pw + 1, ⌈|N|/2⌉), where |N| is the number of nets. It needs one assumption: some net meets some gate.\n- **Multiple folding matches exactly:** with no cap, the minimum number of tracks equals the gate matrix layout cost, which is pw + 1.\n- **Counterexamples:**\n  - On the n × n identity matrix, PLA tracks are exactly ⌈n/2⌉ while pw + 1 = 1. At n = 5 that is 3 against 1, the example item 01 found, and the gap grows without bound as n grows.\n  - The incidence matrix of a path gives the same result on a **connected** graph: pw + 1 ≤ 2, but PLA tracks are at least ⌈(n+1)/2⌉. On the 7-vertex path the gap is at least 2, and it too is unbounded. So restricting Table 1 to connected graphs does not rescue this row.\n\nNot formalised: Möhring's Prop. 3.15 and 3.16, Thm 3.14 in its path-partition wording, and the block/constrained folding variants. The verdict doesn't depend on any of them.\n\n`paper2/equivalences.md` has the updated row 4, the §4 status and a new \"Item 09\" section. PROGRESS.md now reads 9/14, and the item is marked `[x]` in `iterations.md`. Five items remain open, so no LO